# The files that must never be committed here.
#
# This folder is a copy of the owner's live backend folder, and the mistake
# this file exists for is dropping that whole folder in and running
# `git add -A`. It carries his live settings file, the patcher's before-images
# of security-relevant files, transcripts that name his absolute path 231
# times, stale second copies of the entry point, and his databases. None of
# that belongs in a public repository, and once pushed it cannot be taken
# back.
#
# `backend/test_base_matches_repo.py` fails if any of it is ever found here.
# This file is the second line of defence, not the only one.

# His live settings file. The template beside it, jarvis-framework.toml, IS
# committed on purpose: it is the file a new user needs, and it has 23
# settings the live one lacks.
jarvis-framework.toml.backup-*
jarvis-framework.toml.live
*.toml.bak

# The patcher's before-images, and its transcripts.
_jarvis-backup-*/
_jarvis-logs/

# Stale second and third copies of a module.
*.bak
*.before-*

# The pairing token, if one is ever copied here rather than left in Windows
# Credential Manager where it belongs.
token
*.env
cloud-keys.env

# His databases, by name and by the shape one appears under.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite

# Python bytecode. The root .gitignore covers this too; it is repeated because
# this folder is meant to be run in place.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
